    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d9531eb_d19555df",
        "filename": "src/core/SkMaskCache.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T21:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The caching mechanism here previously relied on creating invalid / empty states on the stack, passing in a pointer, and have the \"returned\" object constructed down in the callee. This change cleans this up by doing that with `SkTLazy` to make it super clear that we\u0027re actually constructing these once (instead of a rather confusing amount of mutation).\n\nThis should probably be done by returning the value, but for the sake of changing as little as possible I\u0027m using `SkTLazy`.\n\nThese changes to use `SkTLazy` appear to be responsible for all of the code size increase in this change. It isn\u0027t clear why that is since everything here is in headers and should just all inline to about the same (or even less) code.",
      "revId": "8eb739a668916dc756ace65469eb90b569cfd9e3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
